# React

React is a library for declarative building of UI interfaces.

## Trees

React deals with two trees:

- DOM Tree - normal browser DOM
- React Element Tree - a React's internal structure of the elements, represents the DOM. It's kinda
  a fake/virtual DOM tree. React turns this into a real DOM tree.

An act of _rendering_ is a process of turning React Element Tree into DOM tree.

## Simplest React App

```jsx
const rootNode = document.getElementById("app");
const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(rootNode);
root.render(React.createElement(App));

// custom component
function App() {
  return React.createElement(
    "article",
    null,
    React.createElement("h2", null, "Hello world!"),
  );
}
```
